Design of Oligonucleotide Probes. The first step in any MERFISH experiment. Read full protocol, steps, and materials on protocols.io\" name=\"description\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" rel=\"canonical\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/de/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"de\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"x-default\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/es/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"es\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/fr/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"fr\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/ja/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"ja\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <link href=\"https://www.protocols.io/zh/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" hreflang=\"zh\" rel=\"alternate\" >\n        <meta content=\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes\" property=\"og:title\" >\n        <meta content=\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes. The first step in any MERFISH experiment. Read full protocol, steps, and materials on protocols.io\" property=\"og:description\" >\n        <meta content=\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" property=\"og:url\" >\n        <meta content=\"https://files.protocols.io/external/rujfw26-3B786D04687311F08F960A58A9FEAC02.png\" property=\"og:image\" >\n        <meta content=\"2018-03-29T09:54:07Z\" property=\"article:published_time\" >\n        <meta content=\"Max Brown\" property=\"article:author\" >\n        <meta content=\"summary_large_image\" name=\"twitter:card\" >\n        <meta content=\"@protocolsIO\" name=\"twitter:site\" >\n        <meta content=\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes\" name=\"twitter:title\" >\n        <meta content=\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes. The first step in any MERFISH experiment. Read full protocol, steps, and materials on protocols.io\" name=\"twitter:description\" >\n        <meta content=\"https://files.protocols.io/external/rujfw26-3B786D04687311F08F960A58A9FEAC02.png\" name=\"twitter:image\" >\n        <meta content=\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\" name=\"twitter:url\" >\n        <meta content=\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes\" name=\"citation_title\" >\n        <meta content=\"2018/03/29\" name=\"citation_publication_date\" >\n        <meta content=\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1.pdf\" name=\"citation_pdf_url\" >\n        <meta content=\"Jeffrey R. Moffitt\" name=\"citation_author\" >\n        <meta content=\"Xiaowei Zhuang\" name=\"citation_author\" >\n        <script type=\"application/ld+json\" >{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#org\",\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"height\":\"1550\",\"url\":\"https://www.protocols.io/img/protocols-og.jpg\",\"width\":\"1920\"},\"name\":\"protocols.io\",\"url\":\"https://www.protocols.io/\"}\n        </script>\n        \n        <script type=\"application/ld+json\" >{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#website\",\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"protocols.io\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#org\"},\"url\":\"https://www.protocols.io/\"}\n        </script>\n        \n        <script type=\"application/ld+json\" >{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1#webpage\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"about\":{\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#org\"},\"description\":\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes. The first step in any MERFISH experiment. Read full protocol, steps, and materials on protocols.io\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#website\"},\"name\":\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes\",\"url\":\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1\"}\n        </script>\n        \n        <script type=\"application/ld+json\" >{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1#article\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"affiliation\":\"\",\"name\":\"Max Brown\"},\"dateModified\":\"2018-03-29T09:54:07Z\",\"datePublished\":\"2018-03-29T09:54:07Z\",\"description\":\"The first step in any MERFISH experiment is the design of the oligonucleotide probes that will be used to label individual RNA species. In our current implementation of MERFISH, each oligonucleotide encoding probe consists of three basic components as illustrated in Figure 2. The first region is a 30-nt targeting region that is complementary to a portion of the sequence of the RNA to which it is designed to bind. The second region is a set of sequences that are called readout sequences, which were designed to be complementary and hence only bind to MERFISH readout probes and not other nucleic acid in the cell. Finally, the third region is a set of priming regions used in the construction of these probes, which will be discussed in detail in Probe Construction. In addition to the nucleotide sequences for each of these components, a codebook \u2014the specific set of binary barcodes that will be used and their association with different RNA species of interest\u2014must also be designed. In this section, we provide protocols to design these sequences and to build a codebook. Example code to perform these steps can be found at http://zhuang.harvard.edu/merfish/ .     \",\"headline\":\"RNA Imaging with MERFISH - Design of Oligonucleotide Probes\",\"identifier\":\"10.17504/protocols.io.menc3de\",\"image\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://files.protocols.io/external/rujfw26-3B786D04687311F08F960A58A9FEAC02.png\"},\"keywords\":\"In situ hybridization; RNA; Single cells; Single molecules; Single-molecule imaging; Transcriptomics, rna imaging with merfish, design of the oligonucleotide probe, design of oligonucleotide probe, oligonucleotide probe, merfish readout probe, rna imaging, oligonucleotide, rna, current implementation of merfish, sequence of the rna, nucleotide sequence, first step in any merfish experiment, encoding probe, merfish experiment, rna species, different rna species, other nucleic acid, individual rna species, other nucleic acid in the cell, binary barcode, specific set of binary barcode, readout sequence, merfish, association with different rna species, called readout sequence, addition to the nucleotide sequence, detail in probe construction, barcode, construction of these probe\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/view/rna-imaging-with-merfish-design-of-oligonucleotide-36wgqpn3vk57/v1#webpage\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://www.protocols.io/#org\"}}\n        </script>\n        \n\t\t<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"protocols.io\">\n\t\t<meta name=\"HandheldFriendly\" content=\"True\" />\n\t\t<meta name=\"MobileOptimized\" content=\"320\" />\n\t\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=5.0, user-scalable=yes\" />\n\t\t<meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge\" />\n\t\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#363636\"/>\n\t\t<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content